diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 6a67968..293593c 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -38,6 +38,10 @@ Admins can create, list, inspect, resend, and revoke staff invitations at `/api/
 
 Admins manage and filter users through `/api/v1/users`. Suspended staff lose all sessions and ticket assignments, and the last active admin cannot be suspended. Both admins and agents can use `/api/v1/staff` and update ticket `assignee_id`. Ticket comments accept `public: false` for staff-only private notes; customer request conversations omit those notes. The invitation, preview/acceptance, user, and staff routes are also available without the `/api/v1` prefix for frontend compatibility.
 
+Admins manage department groups and staff memberships through `/api/v1/groups` and `/api/v1/group_memberships`; all staff may browse both resources. Group and membership lists are ordered by ID and membership lists accept `group_id` and `user_id` filters. A staff member can belong to multiple groups, but has exactly one default while memberships remain. Use `PUT /api/v1/group_memberships/:id/make_default` to change it.
+
+Staff tickets expose `group_id` and the group's `id` and `name` in `group`. Ticket lists accept `group_id`, including `group_id=unassigned`. Assigning an ungrouped ticket to staff uses that person's default group when available. Group changes remove assignees who are no longer members, while clearing an assignee leaves the group unchanged and clearing the group clears the assignee. Suspension preserves group memberships.
+
 ## Email support
 
 Action Mailbox accepts RFC 822 messages at `/rails/action_mailbox/relay/inbound_emails` with HTTP basic authentication (`actionmailbox` as the username and `RAILS_INBOUND_EMAIL_PASSWORD` as the password). Customers can send new requests to `<account-subdomain>@<HELPDESK_SUPPORT_DOMAIN>`; `HELPDESK_SUPPORT_DOMAIN` defaults to `support.example.test`. Cc recipients are considered when routing, and messages addressing multiple businesses are ignored.
diff --git a/app/controllers/api/v1/group_memberships_controller.rb b/app/controllers/api/v1/group_memberships_controller.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..af08477
--- /dev/null
+++ b/app/controllers/api/v1/group_memberships_controller.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+module Api
+  module V1
+    class GroupMembershipsController < BaseController
+      before_action :set_current_account
+      before_action :require_active_account
+      before_action :authenticate_user!
+      before_action :require_staff!
+      before_action :require_admin!, only: %i[create destroy make_default]
+      before_action :set_membership, only: %i[show destroy make_default]
+
+      def index
+        scope = current_account.group_memberships.includes(:group, :user).order(:id)
+        scope = scope.where(group_id: id_filter(:group_id)) if params.key?(:group_id)
+        scope = scope.where(user_id: id_filter(:user_id)) if params.key?(:user_id)
+        records, pagination = paginate(scope)
+
+        render json: {
+          group_memberships: records.map { |membership| membership_json(membership) },
+          **pagination
+        }
+      end
+
+      def show
+        render json: { group_membership: membership_json(@membership) }
+      end
+
+      def create
+        attributes = params.require(:group_membership)
+        group_id = attributes.require(:group_id)
+        user_id = attributes.require(:user_id)
+        requested_default = attributes.key?(:default) ? boolean_value(attributes[:default]) : false
+
+        membership = nil
+        current_account.with_lock do
+          membership = GroupMembership.new(
+            group: current_account.groups.find_by(id: group_id),
+            user: current_account.users.find_by(id: user_id),
+            default: requested_default
+          )
+          membership.save!
+        end
+
+        render json: { group_membership: membership_json(membership.reload) }, status: :created
+      end
+
+      def destroy
+        current_account.with_lock { @membership.destroy! }
+        head :no_content
+      end
+
+      def make_default
+        current_account.with_lock { @membership.make_default! }
+
+        render json: { group_membership: membership_json(@membership.reload) }
+      end
+
+      private
+
+      def set_membership
+        @membership = current_account.group_memberships.includes(:group, :user).find(params[:id])
+      end
+
+      def membership_json(membership)
+        GroupMembershipSerializer.new(membership).as_json
+      end
+
+      def id_filter(name)
+        id = Integer(params[name].to_s, 10)
+        return id if id.positive? && id <= (2**63 - 1)
+
+        raise ArgumentError
+      rescue ArgumentError
+        raise ApiRequestError.new(
+          "#{name} must be a positive integer",
+          status: :bad_request,
+          code: "invalid_filter"
+        )
+      end
+
+      def boolean_value(value)
+        return value if value == true || value == false
+
+        case value.to_s.strip.downcase
+        when "true", "1"
+          true
+        when "false", "0"
+          false
+        else
+          raise ApiRequestError.new(
+            "default must be true or false",
+            status: :bad_request,
+            code: "invalid_boolean"
+          )
+        end
+      end
+    end
+  end
+end
